  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), panel seen from its front-left corner and above: guarded T1/T2 to the left, B1-B6 block at the front, encoders E1-E3 to the right, B7-B12 block at the back; the panel is turned about 90 degrees against Virpil's layout sheet",
  "mappingSource": "Virpil support sheet \"VPC Control Panel #1\" (https://support.virpil.com/en/support/solutions/articles/47001250815-vpc-control-panel-1, attachment 47246732385) = the catalog's source; controls identified by the labels printed on the panel (T1-T10, B1-B6, A1, E1-E3 legible on the photo) and by the sheet's layout for B7-B12 and T5-T7",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "T1/T2 are under closed red guards; markers sit on the guard covers. The sheet links A1 and A2 by one leader line to the SLDR and DIAL boxes together, so which knob is SLDR and which DIAL is by order only (A1 = SLDR, as the catalog says). the sheet stacks each toggle's higher number above its lower one (14 over 13, 22 over 21); the catalog calls the lower number \"up\". Which number is the up position is not shown on the sheet; positions are unaffected.",
